ELIZA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
web/js/eliza-rules.js embeds, byte for byte, the DOCTOR script from the
appendix of Joseph Weizenbaum's January 1966 CACM article "ELIZA -- A
Computer Program For the Study of Natural Language Communication Between Man
And Machine". An archive copy is kept at
docs/eliza-original/DOCTOR-1966-CACM.txt.

That transcription is by Anthony Hay, December 2020, from
https://github.com/anthay/ELIZA, released under CC0 1.0 Universal. The
original MAD-SLIP source was recovered from the Weizenbaum archives at MIT
and released into the public domain under CC0 with the agreement of
Weizenbaum's estate; see https://elizagen.org.

CC0 imposes no conditions. The credit here is courtesy, not obligation.
See docs/eliza.md and docs/eliza-original/README.md.

